# the airplay runtime's pins (M4d-D1), read by build-airplay.sh and assemble-airplay-runtime.sh.
#
# source <name> <version> <commit> <url> <sha256>: an upstream release tarball. github publishes no release assets for
# these, so the url is the tag's archive; the sha256 is of that archive, and its pax header names the tagged commit
source shairport-sync 5.6.2 0a34fbda83724cc06266aadcf7c88acc8fef4e7d https://github.com/mikebrady/shairport-sync/archive/refs/tags/5.6.2.tar.gz 0747706e19a64ec550ec8a6a5c26bf8e231a4d032de31644f5a5daa0632c41c4
source nqptp 1.2.9 ab8fb67483411640fd7f1e193889482f2421c37c https://github.com/mikebrady/nqptp/archive/refs/tags/1.2.9.tar.gz 6aa1d73b8ee760bf19378c319db0d0537a867ff961764b150e19f87d96a02210
#
# debsrc <package> <version> <path under https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/> <sha256>: one file of a debian trixie
# source package, from the snapshot below; path and sha256 are apt-get source --print-uris, after apt checked the signed
# InRelease and the Sources index it hashes. avahi is built from debian's (M4d-R5): its orig tarball is upstream's v0.8
# release asset (same sha256), its patches carry the fixes upstream never released, and debian's own avahi-daemon cannot
# run without an avahi user and writes the host's /run/avahi-daemon
debsrc avahi 0.8-16 debian/20261104T212339Z/pool/main/a/avahi/avahi_0.8-16.dsc a8c9a5e3bde8b314b6a2feb385f25fb658bc77960d5f1ed27bc9e159f8691a0a
debsrc avahi 0.8-16 debian/20261104T212339Z/pool/main/a/avahi/avahi_0.8.orig.tar.gz 060309d7a333d38d951bc27598c677af1796934dbd98e1024e7ad8de798fedda
debsrc avahi 0.8-16 debian/20261104T212339Z/pool/main/a/avahi/avahi_0.8-16.debian.tar.xz 2e2f0e6c71186226da0a0a6d93f01dd27a41b6169d4970bbfa3615728fed6d13
#
# deb <arch> <package> <version> <path under https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/> <sha256>: debian trixie, all from
# the snapshot airplay.Dockerfile's apt uses (debian and debian-security at 20261104T212339Z, the base image's own), so
# the build links against these very versions. the path and sha256 are apt-get download --print-uris of each, after
# apt checked the snapshot's signed InRelease files and the Packages indices they hash. exactly the runtime's packages:
# what its programs and libraries need, dbus-daemon itself, gcc-14-base for libatomic1's copyright and base-files for
# the license texts the copyright files point at, and libgcc-s1 on every cpu: glibc loads libgcc_s.so.1 itself when a
# thread is cancelled (shairport sync cancels its player threads at every pause and stream change), so no program
# names it, and without it in lib/ glibc looks in the device's own /lib, which on midi holds 32-bit libraries only
# (shairport then aborts: "libgcc_s.so.1 must be installed for pthread_cancel to work")
deb amd64 base-files 13.8+deb13u7 debian/20261104T212339Z/pool/main/b/base-files/base-files_13.8%2bdeb13u7_amd64.deb fcd42bb5cb63f7bfc4326a92541247872206d60a192fdff65ca14eb83ed408b9
